Data sources (web parity — bound through `SecurityAccessDataSource`, ADR-004; no
networking in the view):
  useVehicles        -> GET /vehicles                         (loadVehicles)
  useSecurityEvents  -> GET /security?vehicle_id              (loadHistory)
  (latest reading)   -> GET /security/latest?vehicle_id       (loadLatest)
  The header VehicleSelect drives `selectedVehicleID` (web useSelectedVehicle); the Range
  presets filter the cached history client-side (web RangePicker/useRangeState). vehicle-list
  failure is the only fatal page error (retryable); latest/history failures stay non-fatal and
  surface the top alert banner while every section still renders (web `anyError`).

SI discipline (ADR-005): a SecurityEvent carries NO SI quantity — every field is a boolean,
an enum string, a timestamp, or a small count. There is therefore nothing to convert; no
non-SI value is stored or computed. Relative timestamps format at the render boundary inside
each composed leaf. The digital twin is a native SwiftUI summary (chips + SF Symbols), never a
WKWebView clone of the web 2D car diagram.

The 8 sections (SummaryStatsRow, SecurityStatusCards, WindowStatusDetail, LiveVehicleState,
SentryModeChart, SecurityStatistics, EventHistoryTable, EventTimeline) are independently-shipped
P4 parity leaves (apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/, same module). The page composes them at
their web positions by projecting one resolved snapshot into each leaf's in-memory relay — the
native parity of the web parent importing + rendering the same components.

